<h2>The order in one view</h2>
<div class="flow">
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Petition disposed of.</strong> The Section 9 petition by the financier against the borrower parties is disposed of at the threshold, not kept pending.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>45 days to act.</strong> The petitioner must commence arbitral proceedings within 45 days of the order.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Automatic sunset.</strong> The interim arrangement continues for those 45 days and vacates automatically if arbitration is not commenced.</div>
  <div class="fstep"><strong>Handover to the tribunal.</strong> If arbitration is commenced, the interim relief continues until the Arbitral Tribunal passes orders under Section 17 — at which point the tribunal&rsquo;s regime replaces the court&rsquo;s.</div>
